 "what": "ROM address -> the gnt4_* wasm IMPORT NAME the staged port units declare for that SDK helper.",
 "why": "research/tools/dolphin-trace/capture_transcript.py `sites` binds a ROM `bl` target to a wasm import by NAME SHAPE (zz_<addr>_ / FUN_<addr>) or by an oracle-registry lookup. The SDK helpers are imported under hand-authored shim names instead (gnt4_PSVECMag_bl, ...) and the registry has no entry for their addresses, so every staged export that calls one was refused as 'binds to no wasm import'. Measured 2026-08-31 over all 810 exports of the 103 staged compile-only units: 115 exports carried such a site, i.e. 14% of the staged surface was unreachable for transcript_green purely for want of this table.",
 "derivation": "Model-free and self-validating. For each staged function, the ORDERED out-of-unit `bl` targets decoded from the ROM are zipped against the ORDERED out-of-unit callee names in the unit's verbatim Ghidra C, only when the two lists have equal length. The zip is ACCEPTED only if every self-describing position (a zz_<addr>_ / FUN_<addr> name) agrees with the ROM target at that position; one disagreement discards the whole function. A function with no self-describing position is discarded in the first pass and re-tested in a second pass using already-accepted entries as induced anchors -- which refuted one function rather than confirming it. A mapping is taken only when the address votes for exactly one name AND that name votes for exactly one address.",
